course: dictionary
lesson: 10583
title: Undercover: secret or sheltered?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Undercover usually means working in secret. A police officer who goes undercover pretends to be someone else to find out information. Spies and undercover reporters do the same thing: they hide who they really are.
explain: Two words, under cover, can mean something very different. «Keep your bike under cover» means put it under a roof or shelter, out of the rain. Read the words around it: bike, shelter, rain. Those clues tell you which meaning fits.
explain: Use the check you already know: swap your meaning into the sentence. Does «the police officer went undercover» make sense with secretly pretending? Yes. Does «keep your bike under cover» make sense with out of the rain? Yes. The clues show you which one is right.
explain: If a sentence has no clues, read the sentences before and after it. A secret, a spy or a crime means the hidden meaning. A bike, a roof or a shed means the sheltered meaning. When you are still unsure, check a dictionary.
fact: Undercover (one word) means working secretly, pretending to be someone else, to find out information.
fact: As an adjective it is used in phrases like «undercover police» or «undercover agents». Go undercover means to start working in this secret way.
fact: Under cover (two words) can mean under a roof or shelter, out of the rain: «Keep your bike under cover.»
fact: Spies, police and reporters can all work undercover.
fact: The words around the word tell you which meaning to choose: secret people or a sheltered place.
exercise: «The detective went undercover to catch the gang.» What does undercover mean here? | Standing under an umbrella in the rain | Sleeping in a tent | *Working in secret, pretending to be someone else | Shouting loudly for help
exercise: «Keep your bike under cover.» What does under cover mean here? | Going very fast down the hill | *Under a roof or shelter, out of the rain | Painted bright red | Hidden in a secret place as a spy
exercise: Which word in «The undercover reporter took notes in the crowd» tells you the reporter was hiding who they really were? | Crowd | Notes | *Undercover | Reporter
test: «The spy went undercover in the enemy city.» What is the spy doing? | Selling old books in a shop | Playing in the park with friends | Sheltering from the rain under a roof | *Working in secret, pretending to be someone else
test: «Please keep the trampoline under cover so it stays dry.» What does under cover mean? | Working secretly to find information | *Under a roof or shelter, out of the rain | Pretending to be a famous singer | Hidden under the bed
exam: Mia reads «The undercover officer waited outside the bank for hours.» What does undercover tell you about the officer? | She was sheltered from the rain under a roof | *She was working in secret, pretending to be someone else | She was lost and looking for her car | She was very tired after a long walk
